From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: request USER_STATS on the host path too

On the host path a station's signal reads 0, with an average of -95 dBm:
the noise floor added to an empty average. 087 updates a peer's PPDU
statistics, RSSI included, only when fc_valid is set, and only the
PPDU_END_USER_STATS TLV sets it. The default monitor status filter does
not request that TLV; ath11k_nss_ext_rx_stats() adds it only with NSS
offload, which is why NSS mode shows a real signal.

Request it in the default filter. NSS mode already runs with exactly this
mask. Three of the five places that restore the default filter (dp_tx.c
and two in debugfs.c) don't go through ath11k_nss_ext_rx_stats(), so
they lose the TLV in NSS mode too; with this they keep it.

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -230,6 +230,7 @@ ath11k_phymodes[NUM_NL80211_BANDS][ATH11
 
 const struct htt_rx_ring_tlv_filter ath11k_mac_mon_status_filter_default = {
 	.rx_filter = HTT_RX_FILTER_TLV_FLAGS_MPDU_START |
+		     HTT_RX_FILTER_TLV_FLAGS_PPDU_END_USER_STATS |
 		     HTT_RX_FILTER_TLV_FLAGS_PPDU_END |
 		     HTT_RX_FILTER_TLV_FLAGS_PPDU_END_STATUS_DONE,
 	.pkt_filter_flags0 = HTT_RX_FP_MGMT_FILTER_FLAGS0,
